<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.theamanullahdev.Paperloom</id>
  <name>Paperloom</name>
  <summary>Play looping videos as your desktop wallpaper</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer id="io.github.theamanullahdev">
    <name>Amanullah Behlim</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Paperloom turns any MP4 loop into a live desktop background — like
      Wallpaper Engine or Lively Wallpaper, but native to the Linux desktop.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Import your own videos or download wallpapers from the built-in online library</li>
      <li>Pauses automatically when a fullscreen app is open, the screen is locked, the battery is low, or a window covers the desktop</li>
      <li>Restores your wallpaper at login</li>
      <li>Designed to use effectively no CPU or memory while the wallpaper isn't visible</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
